          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "I identified the relevant work order as **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070**, for Racine’s September cost period. The analyst-readable record shows that period entered **PENDING_CLOSE at 2025-09-30T18:00:00**.\n\nI could not verify the source transaction or its amount, event-created time, or recorded accounting status: the event rows are not in my accessible source, and both supporting-record resources are restricted to the `records-custodian` role. I therefore cannot calculate how late the event was or conclude whether its recorded status is consistent with Oracle’s policy.\n\nThe supplied Oracle 26B excerpt says that transactions created after Pending Close are not processed until the period is closed or reopened, even if they relate to a current or prior period; it also lists exceptions, including revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. I have not asserted that this policy applies to an event whose details I could not inspect.\n\nNo database records were changed. I submitted the findings as incomplete because the event evidence was unavailable and notified the supervisor of the access limitation.",
